            <div xml:id="d848">

                <pb facs="0834" n="822" xml:id="pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1199/305: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bucknell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-18T13:00:00-05:00">November 18, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 364, November 9, 10 a.m.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“For Thompson from Grady. Please attend December meeting of Economic
                        Committee as my substitute. Advise Stoppani. Letter follows.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>The Department has no objection to Thompson serving in this capacity. You should,
                    in informing Stoppani of Thompson’s selection, state that Thompson, at Grady’s
                    request, will follow the proceedings of the December meeting and report to Grady
                    as his substitute.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
